# No mid-dot separators in UI text

All inline metadata (subtitles, captions, status labels, detail rows, progress text) must separate segments with **exactly three ASCII spaces** (`"   "`), never a middle dot (`·`), bullet (`•`), pipe, or slash.

## Tokens

Use `metadataSeparator` from `@min-apps/design-system/tokens` in JavaScript/TypeScript:

```js
import { metadataSeparator } from '@min-apps/design-system/tokens';
// metadataSeparator === '   '
```

In Swift, join components with `"   "`:

```swift
components.joined(separator: "   ")
```

## Banned patterns

```
" · "          // middle dot (U+00B7)
" • "          // bullet (U+2022)
" | "          // pipe used as metadata separator
.joined(separator: " · ")
```

## Correct examples

```
`${year}   ${genre}`
`${count} movies   ${enriched} enriched`
components.joined(separator: "   ")
```
